        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "abc578e3-b080-5397-a0ba-2a913bd0d8c9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jacques Demy, Paul Sloane, Cary Grant, Stepin Fetchit, Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott, Walter Brennan\n- Works: The Umbrellas of Cherbourg, The Young Girls of Rochefort, Hearts in Dixie, The Woman Accused, The Texans, Break of Day\n- Roles: film directors, writer\n\nFacts:\n- Paul Sloane was born on April 19, 1893, and died on November 15, 1963.\n- Paul Sloane was a writer and film director who directed 26 films from 1925 to 1952 and wrote or co-wrote 35 films.\n- Paul Sloane directed Hearts in Dixie in 1929, and the film featured Stepin Fetchit.\n- Paul Sloane directed The Woman Accused in 1933, and the film featured Cary Grant.\n- Paul Sloane directed The Texans, which featured Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott, and Walter Brennan.\n- Jacques Demy directed The Umbrellas of Cherbourg in 1964 and The Young Girls of Rochefort in 1967.\n- Jacques Demy was best known for the mid-1960s musicals The Umbrellas of Cherbourg and The Young Girls of Rochefort.\n- Break of Day was adapted into a 1980 film directed by Jacques Demy.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "ceeaf48f-f5ba-5308-be23-be3418dd0448",
        "text": "Page: Jacques Demy. Sentence: He is best known for the two musicals he directed in the mid-1960s: \"The Umbrellas of Cherbourg\" (1964) and \"The Young Girls of Rochefort\" (1967).\nPage: Paul Sloane (director). Sentence: Paul Sloane (April 19, 1893 – November 15, 1963) was a writer and film director who directed 26 films from 1925 to 1952, and wrote or co-wrote 35 films.\nPage: Paul Sloane (director). Sentence: His movies include \"Hearts in Dixie\" (1929) with Stepin Fetchit, \"The Woman Accused\" (1933) with Cary Grant, and \"The Texans\" with Joan Bennett, Randolph Scott and Walter Brennan.\nPage: Break of Day. Sentence: It was adapted into a 1980 film directed by Jacques Demy.",
